      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VRChat already strongly deters camera and player movement with its character controllers and SDK, if instead it was made more friendly towards movement of viewpoint and avatars, it would become much easier to do this right without causing discomfort. The current system we have guarantees high likelihood of discomfort by “putting up a fight” every time, because its design did not foresee things like flight and vehicle systems, platform games and even reprojection/optimization schemes. The solution is for VRC to provide us better tools for setting up Correct reprojection and allowing us to move the player gracefully instead of making us fight the SDK for it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-12-15T20:02:07.401Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As Virtual Market has purchased a sponsored spot on the big menus worlds list, I believe there is a certain comfort and performance bar they, and others, should have to attend to for the sponsored spot to be approved.\n\nThis should include, but not be limited to;\n\n- a minimum of 72 fps on the median machine as per the Steam hardware survey & Meta Quest 3/3s\n\n- to not cause discomfort or motion sickness, especially in VR, for example: forcibly manipulating the camera in any way, shape, or form\n\n- ensuring all content is safe for work and does not violate VRChat's terms of use\n\nA prime example of the second point is VKet's \"2025 W Nostalgia Storybook\" (https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_3d2caab1-f16c-4b01-80a2-7dbb1fe814d4)\n\nThis world forcibly takes control over the camera and can cause significant motion sickness. The world contains no warning it will do this, with no obvious option to skip or disable the forced camera view.",
